 "Notice that we are given an equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y).\n$$\n\nThis is an autonomous equation because the right-hand side is a function of $y$ only. This means that, for a fixed value of $y,$ the slope does not vary with $x.$ \n\nOf the given slope fields, the only one that varies with $x$ for a fixed value of $y$ is the following:\n\n  \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/assets/9f883ac23f1a6574f2afdf2ca4dcb0aaf617c992c6c67f34ca5d3a0af63b8149.png)\n\n \n\nTo see this more clearly, notice that if we draw a horizontal line, the slopes touching the line vary as we go left and right along the line. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/assets/b157285c42bd83c28ed4b3da51fa6d0e83353ae806781fd4231abd45da880228.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-98018/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c9b15835-9882-5758-b5ee-924ba48f7efb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-98018"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-119301/selection/e7dbc60ebda62017e83256b0433f80519735b2e2ead51e3616cec22126b0e88c" :answer/id #uuid "c30505a8-717e-5634-b050-384bf3e3b194" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/assets/023176867db863a881be740801ca9607498e26b164b9009be6669527a02974ed.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119301/selection/9e2c968e07741a1af68724da3fdcbed7a3dcce8f869447af6f119b6098f7f2d3" :answer/id #uuid "71aae8f1-9717-5b47-b5c7-f0e1cdf4bb6e" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/assets/710e198c7575ea546e78101b46f23e9170aa6f4770cdb1bf4010ff7fa8b9107e.png" :db/ensure [:answe