date]} {:db/id "q-119301" :question/id #uuid "da26896c-6811-50e9-b31a-f7fc298f1418" :question/math-academy-id "q-119301" :question/problem "Which of the following could be the slope field for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y)?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we are given an equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y).\n$$\n\nThis is an autonomous equation because the right-hand side is a function of $y$ only. This means that, for a fixed value of $y,$ the slope does not vary with $x.$ \n\nOf the given slope fields, the only one that does not vary with $x$ for a fixed value of $y$ is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/assets/1497231f27da97063782fa93592b038676810b2d8cc0ad89bb97522b7348a3d5.png)\n\n  \n\nTo see this more clearly, notice that if we draw a horizontal line, the slopes touching the line do not vary as we move left and right along the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/assets/0ba4cdd42093e6341f0ec89d56c332b1de4bf6794aeae1f3fd4f77e343bb5f59.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-119301/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c9b15835-9882-5758-b5ee-924ba48f7efb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-119301"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-119300/selection/51c285c1e7caa8c0e45f1a4ec2ceef15e8ebda7132066041661fa31aa516ffdb" :answer/id #uuid "b0fd1eba-c09c-5e34-9e98-f6511710ceaa" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/assets/60320829f744c54b2a299a2c2c7cb9665365e8a5617c9e53f1aa5dffd52ec5a2.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119300/selection/c9184bb26a22ddfdbee276b1ca2c3e9e6051f5e339a0043b7cc5606f9ec0c324" :answer/id #